{"id":"CVE-2018-0732","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"openssl","published":"2018-06-12T13:00:00.000Z","updated":"2026-10-08T21:13:55.704Z","title":"Client DoS due to large DH parameter","description":"During key agreement in a TLS handshake using a DH(E) based ciphersuite a malicious server can send a very large prime value to the client. This will cause the client to spend an unreasonably long period of time generating a key for this prime resulting in a hang until the client has finished. This could be exploited in a Denial Of Service attack. Fixed in OpenSSL 1.1.0i-dev (Affected 1.1.0-1.1.0h). Fixed in OpenSSL 1.0.2p-dev (Affected 1.0.2-1.0.2o).","cwe":["Client side Denial of Service"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","other":"unknown","content":"{\"lang\": \"eng\", \"url\": \"https://www.openssl.org/policies/secpolicy.html#Low\", \"value\": \"Low\"}"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"yes","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"OpenSSL","product":"OpenSSL","versions":["affected Fixed in OpenSSL 1.1.0i-dev (Affected 1.1.0-1.1.0h)","affected Fixed in OpenSSL 1.0.2p-dev (Affected 1.0.2-1.0.2o)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2018/07/msg00043.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[debian-lts-announce] 20180728 [SECURITY] [DLA 1449-1] openssl security update"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/104442","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"104442"},{"url":"https://www.debian.org/security/2018/dsa-4355","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_DEBIAN"],"name":"DSA-4355"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2018:2552","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2018:2552"},{"url":"https://security.gentoo.org/glsa/201811-03","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_GENTOO"],"name":"GLSA-201811-03"},{"url":"https://usn.ubuntu.com/3692-2/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-3692-2"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/