{"id":"CVE-2018-0737","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"openssl","published":"2018-04-16T17:00:00.000Z","updated":"2026-10-15T17:19:17.232Z","title":"Cache timing vulnerability in RSA Key Generation","description":"The OpenSSL RSA Key generation algorithm has been shown to be vulnerable to a cache timing side channel attack. An attacker with sufficient access to mount cache timing attacks during the RSA key generation process could recover the private key. Fixed in OpenSSL 1.1.0i-dev (Affected 1.1.0-1.1.0h). Fixed in OpenSSL 1.0.2p-dev (Affected 1.0.2b-1.0.2o).","cwe":["Constant time issue"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","other":"unknown","content":"{\"lang\": \"eng\", \"url\": \"https://www.openssl.org/policies/secpolicy.html#Low\", \"value\": \"Low\"}"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"OpenSSL","product":"OpenSSL","versions":["affected Fixed in OpenSSL 1.1.0i-dev (Affected 1.1.0-1.1.0h)","affected Fixed in OpenSSL 1.0.2p-dev (Affected 1.0.2b-1.0.2o)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2018/07/msg00043.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[debian-lts-announce] 20180728 [SECURITY] [DLA 1449-1] openssl security update"},{"url":"https://www.debian.org/security/2018/dsa-4355","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_DEBIAN"],"name":"DSA-4355"},{"url":"https://usn.ubuntu.com/3628-2/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-3628-2"},{"url":"https://security.gentoo.org/glsa/201811-21","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_GENTOO"],"name":"GLSA-201811-21"},{"url":"https://usn.ubuntu.com/3692-2/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-3692-2"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2018:3505","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2018:3505"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/103766","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"103766"},{"url":"https://usn.ubuntu