{"id":"CVE-2018-16395","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2018-11-16T18:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-05T10:24:32.106Z","description":"An issue was discovered in the OpenSSL library in Ruby before 2.3.8, 2.4.x before 2.4.5, 2.5.x before 2.5.2, and 2.6.x before 2.6.0-preview3. When two OpenSSL::X509::Name objects are compared using ==, depending on the ordering, non-equal objects may return true. When the first argument is one character longer than the second, or the second argument contains a character that is one less than a character in the same position of the first argument, the result of == will be true. This could be leveraged to create an illegitimate certificate that may be accepted as legitimate and then used in signing or encryption operations.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://www.ruby-lang.org/en/news/2018/10/17/openssl-x509-name-equality-check-does-not-work-correctly-cve-2018-16395/","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2018:3738","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2018:3738"},{"url":"https://www.ruby-lang.org/en/news/2018/11/06/ruby-2-6-0-preview3-released/","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2018:3729","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2018:3729"},{"url":"https://hackerone.com/reports/387250","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2018:3730","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2018:3730"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2018:3731","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2018:3731"},{"url":"https://www.ruby-lang.org/en/news/2018/10/17/ruby-2-3-8-released/","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://www.debian.org/security/2018/dsa-4332","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_DEBIAN"],"name":"DSA-4332"},{"url":"https://usn.ubuntu.com/3808-1/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-3808-1"},{"url":"https://www.ruby-lang.org/en/news/2018/10/17/ruby-2-4-5-released/","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20190221-0002/","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://www.ruby-lang.org/en/news/2018/10/17/ruby-2-5-2-released/","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2018/10/msg00020.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[debian-lts-announce] 20181028 [SECURITY] [DLA 1558-1] ruby2.1 security update"},{"url":"http://www.securitytracker.com/id/1042105","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_SECTRACK"],"name":"1042105"},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-security-announce/2019-07/msg00036.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"openSUSE-SU-2019:1771"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2019:1948","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2019:1948"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2019:2565","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2019:2565"},{"url":"https://www.oracle.com/security-alerts/cpujan2020.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["openssl"]}
